Package: fdatestcpp
Type: Package
Title: Fast Interval-Wise and Threshold-Wise Tests for Functional Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Matteo", family = "Fontana",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mtt.fnt@gmail.com"),
    person(given = "Alessia", family = "Pini", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "author of 'fdatest', whose procedures and code are ported"),
    person(given = "Aymeric", family = "Stamm", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "contributor to and maintainer of 'fdatest', whose procedures and code are ported"),
    person(given = "Simone", family = "Vantini", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "author of 'fdatest', whose procedures and code are ported"))
Description: Implements fast versions of the interval-wise testing procedure
    of Pini and Vantini (2017) <doi:10.1080/10485252.2017.1306627> and of the
    threshold-wise testing procedure of Abramowicz et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1111/biom.13669> for one- and two-sample tests on functional data,
    following their implementation in the development version of the
    'fdatest' package (<https://github.com/permaverse/fdatest>). Curves can be
    given as matrices or as 'fda' functional data objects. Resampling uses sign
    flips, paired swaps or label permutations, optionally constant within
    blocks of observations, or user-supplied resamples. Results can be
    plotted with 'ggplot2', with the selected domain shaded. The interval-wise
    adjustment costs O(B p^2) operations instead of O(B p^3) for B resamples
    and p grid points. With the same inputs and random seed, the p-values
    reproduce those of that 'fdatest' version exactly on platforms where R
    and the compiler use the same long double precision.
